#29801
"Overgrown Trail Through a Forest - A Pair of Mushrooms"
"The trail turns here, leading west toward a road in the distance and to the

south through a pair of violet-leaved ferns.  Undergrowth and grass encroaches

upon the trail, threatening to conceal the dirt path from sight.  Shrubs of

dark green buds and black-violet flowers, scarlet, diamond-petaled blossoms,

and stout brown trees line the trail.  Pale green grass struggles to survive

with the meager sunlight it receives on either side of the trail.  A pair of

bulbous gray mushrooms sit beside one of the taller trees.

"
