#29802
"Overgrown Trail Through a Forest - Before a Glade"
"The shadowy trail disappears to the south as it approaches a glade in the

forest.  To the north it continues further into the wet, leafy forest.  The

moist dirt trail gives way to short @ggreen@n grasses and other unrecognizable

plants.  Stout trees, with wide, soft-barked trunks line the trail.  They lack

any low-lying branches, all of their boughs growing at the trees' crowns,

forming a low canopy of dark @ggreen@n leaves.  Pockmarked and knotted, the trees

stand as grisly sentinels for the vast forest behind.

"
