#29803
"The Low Grasses of a Glade"
"A sweeping field covers this glade in peculiar green grasses.  The short

grasses here have unusual violet veins running up their centers, giving the

area a strange organic contrast.  A few strangers to the glade, jagged-leaved

weeds and spotted mushrooms, dot the landscape.  To the south, the grasses

seem to flourish and begin to lengthen, while to the north, they recede in the

place of a trail that leads into the forest.  To the east and west, the short

grassed section of the glade continues.

"
