#29804
"A Patch of Wild Flowers"
"Near the northwest corner of this grassy glade, a patch of wild flowers has

sprung up, rife with pale yellow buds and thorny stems.  Several of the

flowers have begun to blossom, and their satiny petals are golden and pointed.

In the center of each flower, encircled by its petals, its filaments form a

heart of crimson.  The glade opens to the south and east, while to the

northwest the wet woodlands prevent further travel in that direction.

"
