#29805
"A Clover Patch in the Glade"
"A dark patch of clover covers much of the ground here, in the midst of the

short @ggreen@n grasses covering the glade.  The tiny, three-leaved plants

dominate the area, seeming like a swarming army of blossoming soldiers.  To

the north, stout trees sit beside leafy bushes and budding shrubs, preventing

further travel in that direction.  Westward, the short grasses of the glade

continue, while southward high grasses obscure vision.  A colorful patch of

flowers lies in the distance to the east.

"
