#29806
"Near a Flower Bed"
"Near the northeast of the glade here is a carefully tended flower bed.  The

bed is rectangular, with five sections of exotic plants - one at each corner

and a fifth in the center.  Short-stemmed blackbuds comprise one corner, and

across from them grow white daffodils.  In another corner, red carnations are

growing, and opposite them, blue violets stab out of the dark earth.  In the

center, black-stemmed greenwings form a circular section.  The outer forest to

the northeast hems in the glade, which opens up to the south and west.

"
