quiver with only a hint of life, and the quiet rustle within resonates with an

inaudible sense of the sublime.  The high grasses of the glade lie languidly

under the guard of the forest.  A single blossoming flower, nearly out of

sight in the forest to the south, bends questioningly in an unseen breeze.

The open glade lies to the east and north.

