#29808
"A Fringe of Whispering Trees"
"Whispers of an unknown nature seep into the glade from the forest to the

southwest.  Like the shudder of a bat's wings, or the breathy heave of a man

at his end, the murmurs attack you with silent @Rmalevolence@n.  Yet, the soft,

cherubic trees stand unwittingly at the forest's edge; the ferns are noiseless

and rest without motion.  West from here is a quiet corner in the glade.

Further south the land begins to rise gradually, while to the north the grass

shortens noticeably.  To the east is more high grass.

"
