from the skin of the earth, the cascading limbs ebb and sway in harmony.  The

ground is not even visible beneath the sea of vegetation, and only a handful

of weeds break the continuity of grass.  The high grasses continue to the east

and west, and the glade begins to rise to the south.  Northward are shorter

grasses and a distant trail into the forest.

