#29810
"The Edge of a Peculiar Forest"
"To the east lies an expanse of forest constituted of numerous odd plants and

varieties of vegetation.  From here, you can see several extraordinary

examples.  One shrub with hourglass-shaped petals grows near the edge of the

glade.  A tall, limbless red tree with deeply grooved bark rests beside it.

Several bushes with bowed branches and silvery buds grow deeper in the forest.

Strange blue moss crawls up one side of the trees, nearly to their tops.  High

grass grows here, to the west, and to the south.  To the north you can make

out a colorful flower bed.

