#29813
"The Slick Grasses of a Glade"
"The grasses here are wet with moisture.  A rocky rise to the south leads to a

shallow pool.  The rocks, themselves wet with condensation, green with moss,

and buried in the mud, dot the incline.  The grasses are slick and

treacherous, and even the ground beneath, rarely visible, provides precarious

footing at best.  Eastward, a rotting log lies in the distance near the

neighboring woods.  South is the pool, and to the north and west are more high

grasses.

"
