#29815
"In a Glade - A Growth of Mushrooms"
"Countless mushrooms grow here, though they are of only a few distinguishable

varieties.  Some of the mushrooms are a deep gray color, spotted on their caps

with a pale yellow coloring.  These are the biggest and most abundant of the

varieties.  Another is a tan color with ribbed caps, taller than the others

but fewest in number.  The last are a deep red color with thin white strands

hanging down like the tentacles of a jellyfish.  North of here, the glade

descends slightly over a rocky decline.  To the south, a lone tree is visible.

To the west, a dense forest blocks travel, while to the east the grassy glade

opens up.

"
