#29816
"The Quiet Grasses of a Glade"
"The light green grasses of the glade sit here, barely stirring.  They live and

die with less than a murmur, even the smallest rustle foreign to these little

beasts.  Lacking a voice, yet not desiring one, the grasses live their lives

catching wind, catching light, and warming the earth.  East of here there lies

a shallow pool.  To the east down a decline or to the south continuing

alongside the pool, the grassy glade continues.  Westward lies an enormous

mushroom patch.

"
