#29817
"In a Shallow Pool of Water"
"A clear pool of water has collected here in a shallow depression in the glade.

No more than a few inches deep, beneath the water lies sunken detritus and a

muddy bottom.  A variety of curious looking plants hang over the water's edge;

some budded weeds lap at the water, and some pale @Yyellow@n flowers seem to be

peering into its meager depths.  This water-filled depression sits on the top

of a hill that extends to the east and south.  To the north, a slight decline

leads into high grasses.  To the west, you can climb out of the pool onto dry

land.

"
