#29819
"A Fringe of Brush and Bees"
"The forest to the west encroaches upon the glade here.  Between two stout,

green trees is a thatch of dark reddish bushes.  Budding green, the crimson-

barked bushes are tangled in a wild mess of branches.  A swarm of irreverent

bees flies in and out of the thicket in a frenzy.  The small, black and gold

insects seem to have a preoccupation with these plants.  High grasses grow

here, curling curiously at their tips.  In all directions but west these

grasses continue.

"
