#29822
"In a Shallow Pool of Water - Near a Dense Forest"
"The edge of an imposing forest stands over a clear pool of water here.  The

pool, no more than a few inches deep, sitting in a depression in the ground,

is being fed by a burbling spring at the edge of the forest.  The forest to

the east is particularly dense and green, fed as it is by copious amounts of

water from the spring.  Out of immediate sight, however, a foreboding darkness

covers the forest in gloom.  The pool lies still to the north and west, and to

the south is the southeasternmost corner of the glade.

