#29825
"The Wet Grounds of a Green Glade"
"The long grass of the glade lies low to the ground, weighted by beads of clear

water.  The entire area is wet, the ground beneath muddy, moist, and quick to

give under any pressure.  Near the forest bordering the glade to the south, it

appears to dry up a bit, while near a pool to the north it is the most wet.  A

few branches have fallen from the canopy of the trees to the south and lie

half buried in the ground.  To the west and east, the glade's grasses

continue, while to the north a pool rests in a depression in the glade.

