#29827
"The March of Trees"
"Tree upon tree lines the trail here, standing as if sentinels for the wooded

depths beyond.  They seem to be evenly spaced, and each tree on one side of

the path has a complement on the other side.  Between the trees, budding,

black-barked bushes sit unmoving in the dim light.  Small patches of grass

claw their way out from fallen leaves on the forest's floor.  This uniform

aberration exists only for a short way before returning to the regular

irregularity of the forest to the east and west.

"
