#29834
"The Creek Runs By"
"A faintly burbling creek runs by from the west and out of sight down a pitch

in the forest to the east.  This narrow trail follows alongside it for some

distance before turning south.  A centipede is crawling up one of the soft-

barked mironas, his movement alike the rise and fall of mountains: the

crushing upheaval of earth and the hasty descent to platitude.  Thorny vines

strangle black barked bushes with their long tendrils.  Leaves and detritus

litter the forest's floor.

"
