#29850
"Parting Shadows"
"Dark shadows creep across the ground, tiny fingers of absentia in the forest.

This tract of dismal forest is dark and gloomy, but its shadows are sharp and

marked.  Their contrast with the light is remarkable, making them almost

foreign, and perhaps it is the lighter soil here that is at fault.  The pale

tan dirt and sand mixture that forms the trail is clear as it turns a corner

east and south, but the periphery of striking shadows is distracting.  A

staccato silence marks the intervals between sounds, and everything here seems

strangely amplified and otherworldly.

